{"type":"text","timestamp":1788226257067,"sessionID":"ses_fa570bfb2ffeDnSgXdchLkmauU","part":{"id":"prt_05a972533001L44HneQTb55EY4","messageID":"msg_05a971fab001D55dZP0Vb5zLc7","sessionID":"ses_fa570bfb2ffeDnSgXdchLkmauU","type":"text","text":"Done. Everything TASK.md asks for is implemented and verified:\n\n**Deliverables**\n- `app.py` — Books REST API using only the Python standard library (`http.server` + `sqlite3`, per `stack.json`'s \"stdlib\" framework): `POST/GET /books` (with `?author=` filter), `GET/PUT/DELETE /books/{id}`, and `GET /health`. Title/author are required (non-empty strings), year must be an integer, isbn a string. Status codes: 201 (+`Location`), 200, 204, 400 with error details, 404, 405 (+`Allow`). DB path configurable via `BOOKS_DB` env var; `HOST`/`PORT` also supported.\n- `tests/test_app.py` — 27 tests: unit tests for the storage and validation layers, plus integration tests that run the real threaded HTTP server and exercise every endpoint.\n- `README.md` — setup, run, env vars, endpoint table, curl examples, test instructions.\n\n**Verification**\n- `pytest tests` → 27 passed (also passes under `python -m unittest discover`)\n- Live smoke test with curl: create (201), validation failure (400), list/filter, get (200/404), update, delete (204), method-not-allowed (405) all correct.","time":{"start":1788226250035,"end":1788226257063}}}
